    (property "Assembly" "hand" (at 243.84 187.96 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Note" "A MATCHED PAIR with its twin (owner, 2026-10-03: 'Tighten cap matching'; 68 pF since #32): C-CM-IN+ and C-CM-IN- from one reel of the 1 % C0G part, measured on one LCR meter (open-circuit compensated, at 100 kHz if it has it) and fitted together only when each is within 0.5 % of the pair's mean. Their mismatch converts the umbilical's common mode in proportion to frequency, so it sets each bandwidth mode's CMRR at its top (module/breath-receive-stage/sim cmrr-*). The 1 % C0G is the tightest catalogued, so the match is made by hand: fitted by hand, after measuring. Fixed in every mode of the bandwidth toggle" (at 243.84 187.96 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
